#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/Interfaces-Topics-Services-Actions.rst:18
msgid "Interfaces (topics, services, actions)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/Interfaces-Topics-Services-Actions.rst:21
msgid ""
"Topics, services, and actions in ROS define how nodes exchange data. This "
"article explains these different types of ROS interface and the differences "
"between them. With this information, you'll be able to select the right "
"interface for your purposes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/Interfaces-Topics-Services-Actions.rst:31
msgid "Table of Contents"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/Interfaces-Topics-Services-Actions.rst:43
msgid "Summary"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/Interfaces-Topics-Services-Actions.rst:45
msgid ""
"ROS nodes typically communicate through the following three types of "
"interfaces:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/Interfaces-Topics-Services-Actions.rst:47
msgid ":doc:`Topics <interfaces/About-Topics>`: For continuous data streams."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/Interfaces-Topics-Services-Actions.rst:48
msgid ""
":doc:`Services <interfaces/About-Services>`: For request/response "
"interactions (short tasks that return a result quickly)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/Interfaces-Topics-Services-Actions.rst:49
msgid ""
":doc:`Actions <interfaces/About-Actions>`: For long-running tasks with "
"feedback (tasks that may take some time to complete)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/Interfaces-Topics-Services-Actions.rst:51
msgid ""
"For consistent communication, each interface uses definitions provided in "
"``.msg``, ``.srv``, or ``.action`` files. To learn more about the interface "
"definitions, see :doc:`interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Interface-"
"specifications`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/Interfaces-Topics-Services-Actions.rst:55
msgid "Topics"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/Interfaces-Topics-Services-Actions.rst:57
msgid ""
"The topic interface is meant for continuous data streams, such as streaming "
"sensor data or the status of your robot. Topic definitions are stored in "
"``.msg`` files. Topics implement a publish/subscribe pattern. A node "
"publishes data to a topic, and other nodes subscribe to receive that data."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/Interfaces-Topics-Services-Actions.rst:62
#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/Interfaces-Topics-Services-Actions.rst:108
#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/Interfaces-Topics-Services-Actions.rst:133
msgid "This interface type has the following main characteristics:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/Interfaces-Topics-Services-Actions.rst:64
msgid ""
"Communication is asynchronous and one-way. The publisher decides when data "
"is sent. Data might be published and subscribed at any time, independent of "
"any senders/receivers. Callbacks receive data when it is available."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/Interfaces-Topics-Services-Actions.rst:68
msgid "Multiple publishers and subscribers can share the same topic."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/Interfaces-Topics-Services-Actions.rst:77
msgid ""
"Topic keys identify individual publishers on a topic so nodes and tools can "
"distinguish where messages come from. Each topic key makes it easier to "
"track data sources when several publishers share the same topic."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/Interfaces-Topics-Services-Actions.rst:81
msgid "Topic statistics"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/Interfaces-Topics-Services-Actions.rst:82
msgid ""
"Topic statistics are built-in measurements that help you understand how "
"messages behave when a subscription receives them. When enabled, they "
"automatically track two things:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/Interfaces-Topics-Services-Actions.rst:0
msgid "Message age"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/Interfaces-Topics-Services-Actions.rst:85
msgid "How old a message is when it arrives, based on its timestamp."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/Interfaces-Topics-Services-Actions.rst:0
msgid "Message period"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/Interfaces-Topics-Services-Actions.rst:86
msgid "The time between incoming messages."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/Interfaces-Topics-Services-Actions.rst:88
msgid ""
"For both message age and period, ROS calculates the average, minimum, "
"maximum, standard deviation, and the number of samples, using a moving "
"window that updates every time a new message arrives. These calculations run "
"in constant time and memory using the dedicated utilities. When you enable "
"topic statistics for a subscription, ROS publishes the collected data at "
"regular intervals as a ``MetricsMessage`` on a statistics topic. This gives "
"you a clear view of timing patterns, delays, and irregularities, making it "
"easier to assess system performance or diagnose problems related to the "
"message flow."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/Interfaces-Topics-Services-Actions.rst:95
msgid ""
"The default interval is 1 second. The default statistics topic is ``/"
"statistics``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/Interfaces-Topics-Services-Actions.rst:98
msgid ""
":doc:`Learn how to enable topic statistics <../Developer-Tools/Introspection-"
"and-analysis/Topic-Statistics-Tutorial/Topic-Statistics-Tutorial>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/Interfaces-Topics-Services-Actions.rst:101
msgid "Services"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/Interfaces-Topics-Services-Actions.rst:103
msgid ""
"The service interface is meant for request/response interactions, for "
"example, when you want to send a query requesting the configuration of a "
"specific robot. Service definitions are stored in ``.srv`` files. Services "
"implement a request/response pattern. A client sends a request, and a server "
"replies with a response."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/Interfaces-Topics-Services-Actions.rst:110
msgid ""
"Communication is two-way: each request receives one response. Client "
"libraries let you wait for the response asynchronously, or block until it "
"arrives. Blocking on a service call from inside a callback can deadlock your "
"node. See :doc:`interfaces/services/Working-with-services/Sync-Vs-Async`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/Interfaces-Topics-Services-Actions.rst:114
msgid ""
"Services are ideal for remote procedure calls that terminate quickly and "
"return a result or confirmation, such as querying the state of a node or "
"doing a quick calculation such as IK."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/Interfaces-Topics-Services-Actions.rst:115
msgid ""
"Services should not be used for longer running processes, in particular "
"processes that might need to be preempted if exceptional situations occur. "
"Use an action instead."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/Interfaces-Topics-Services-Actions.rst:127
msgid "Actions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/Interfaces-Topics-Services-Actions.rst:129
msgid ""
"The action interface is meant for long-running tasks with feedback, for "
"example, moving a robot to a specific position, or asking the robot to "
"perform a complex motion. Action definitions are stored in ``.action`` "
"files. Actions allow clients to send goals, receive feedback during the "
"execution, cancel if needed, and return a result when the goal finishes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/Interfaces-Topics-Services-Actions.rst:135
msgid ""
"Communication is asynchronous, with feedback during execution and a final "
"result."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/Interfaces-Topics-Services-Actions.rst:136
msgid ""
"Actions are suitable for any discrete behavior that takes time and provides "
"feedback during execution, such as moving a robot, slow perception routines "
"that take several seconds to terminate, or initiating a lower-level control "
"mode."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/Interfaces-Topics-Services-Actions.rst:137
msgid ""
"Actions can be preempted (cancelled) and preemption should always be "
"implemented cleanly by action servers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/Interfaces-Topics-Services-Actions.rst:138
msgid ""
"Actions can keep state for the lifetime of a goal. If executing two action "
"goals in parallel on the same server, a separate state instance can be kept "
"for each client because the goal is uniquely identified by its ID."
msgstr ""

