#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/Interfaces-Topics-Services-Actions.rst:177
msgid "What are the three primary ROS interface types?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/Interfaces-Topics-Services-Actions.rst:178
msgid ""
"Topics, services, and actions. Topics suit continuous data streams, services "
"suit short request/response interactions, and actions suit long-running "
"tasks that provide feedback."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/Interfaces-Topics-Services-Actions.rst:181
msgid "When should I use a topic?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/Interfaces-Topics-Services-Actions.rst:182
msgid ""
"Use a topic for continuous, asynchronous data streams such as sensor data or "
"robot state. Topics use a publish/subscribe pattern, and multiple publishers "
"and subscribers can share the same topic."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/Interfaces-Topics-Services-Actions.rst:185
msgid "When should I use a service?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/Interfaces-Topics-Services-Actions.rst:186
msgid ""
"Use a service for a short request/response interaction that returns a result "
"quickly, such as querying configuration or running a quick calculation. Do "
"not use services for long-running processes that might need to be cancelled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/Interfaces-Topics-Services-Actions.rst:189
msgid "When should I use an action?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/Interfaces-Topics-Services-Actions.rst:190
msgid ""
"Use an action for a longer-running task that may need feedback during "
"execution, such as moving a robot to a pose. Actions let a client send a "
"goal, receive feedback, cancel if needed, and get a final result."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/Interfaces-Topics-Services-Actions.rst:193
msgid "Which interface types support cancellation?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/Interfaces-Topics-Services-Actions.rst:194
msgid "Only actions support cancellation. Topics and services do not."
msgstr ""
